meta {
  name: Get
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/web/npp/boxoverzicht?scan={{nppBoxScan}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Auth-Token: {{authToken}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.bonnr: isNumber
  res.body.groepnr: isNumber
  res.body.klant: isString
  res.body.opmerking: isString
  res.body.empty: isBoolean
  res.body.articles: isArray
}

docs {
  GET /web/npp/boxoverzicht?scan=<rawScanValue> - given a raw scanned box
  label (e.g. "B12345-1" or "12345-1"), returns the bon header
  (bonnr/groepnr/klant), a status remark (opmerking - from bon_led.opm,
  bonnr/groepnr/led_lijn=0/lijnnr=90, or the literal "niets" if there is
  none), and the aggregated article list (bonlijn.gereserv summed per
  artnr, applying the exact same include/exclude filter as the legacy
  N:\LunaV12\NPP\NPPBoxView.w vul-temptable procedure) for that bon/groep.

  An empty box (bon exists, but zero bonlijn rows match the filter for
  that groepnr) is NOT an error - it comes back 200 with "empty": true
  and "articles": [].

  {{nppBoxScan}} must be set (collection/environment variable, not
  currently in Local.bru) to a real "<bonnr>-<groepnr>" (or
  "B<bonnr>-<groepnr>") scan value from LunaNew for a bon/groep that
  actually has matching bonlijn rows, to exercise the non-empty case.

  Read-only - backed by Backend/src/Luna/Web/NPPBoxOverzichtHandler.cls +
  Luna/BusinessLogic/NPPBoxOverzichtBE.cls.
}
